00:37:32.069 --> 00:37:34.819
How do you guys prepare for those first cold calls for

00:37:34.819 --> 00:37:38.880
today? Are there with investors or with companies that you

00:37:38.900 --> 00:37:41.900
got may minor interest, did you talk to people, did you just

00:37:41.900 --> 00:37:43.900
kind of fill PowerPoint presentations like actual meeting

00:37:43.900 --> 00:37:44.929
with them?

00:37:44.949 --> 00:37:50.009
So I just did what I did for 4.5 years. I don't do cold

00:37:50.029 --> 00:37:54.529
calls. I deliberately try and get someone into somebody else

00:37:54.549 --> 00:37:57.869
because it changes everything you do it that way. But there

00:37:57.889 --> 00:38:02.949
were times when we had to do a cold call, in fact one of the

00:38:02.969 --> 00:38:05.929
customers that we work with on a regular basis, I cold

00:38:05.949 --> 00:38:09.309
emailed, the CIO of Fortune 100 Company and he responded and

00:38:09.329 --> 00:38:12.569
we had a meeting and he responded and we had a meeting. That

00:38:12.569 --> 00:38:18.119
was very tricky the first line was a GSB grad and that helps

00:38:18.139 --> 00:38:23.489
a lot, they will take a meeting. So that's how I start the

00:38:23.509 --> 00:38:26.819
meetings, and that's how I get the meetings if you will. I

00:38:26.839 --> 00:38:29.339
try and work through someone and that's the most effective

00:38:29.339 --> 00:38:32.839
way if we can do it. LinkedIn is a fantastic way to go about

00:38:32.839 --> 00:38:35.839
that. So you can see who knows that somebody else and then

00:38:35.839 --> 00:38:39.089
if it really comes down to a cold e-mail you really want to

00:38:39.089 --> 00:38:41.839
just make yourself seem credible in the first line, and be

00:38:41.839 --> 00:38:44.839
really clear with them exactly what you want and if you are

00:38:44.839 --> 00:38:47.839
trying to get feedback you should be very clear that you are

00:38:47.839 --> 00:38:50.839
just trying to get feedback and not trying to sell them a

00:38:50.839 --> 00:38:53.839
product. If you are trying to sell him a product, be clear

00:38:53.839 --> 00:38:57.089
in that because if you are kind of vague they don't want to

00:38:57.089 --> 00:38:59.839
deal with that. In terms of the meeting I always have

00:38:59.839 --> 00:39:03.409
PowerPoint, all my meetins are on WebEx and you know I keep

00:39:03.429 --> 00:39:06.179
my PowerPoint as clean and as simple as humanly possible but

00:39:06.179 --> 00:39:08.929
at least for us what we are doing a sufficiently complex

00:39:08.929 --> 00:39:12.339
where I need a diagram to just convey the concepts fast

00:39:12.359 --> 00:39:16.860
enough we can get a lot of time. In terms of time I limit

00:39:16.880 --> 00:39:20.269
everything to 20-minute meetings. Anything past that they

00:39:20.289 --> 00:39:23.489
start with Nancy they may not take the meeting, and I tell

00:39:23.509 --> 00:39:26.509
him upfront in e-mail and I tell him upfront in the actual

00:39:26.509 --> 00:39:29.259
meeting that it's going to be 20 minutes so that everybody

00:39:29.259 --> 00:39:32.489
is kind of cool. And then I just have really clear idea of

00:39:32.489 --> 00:39:35.239
what I want out of the meetings, what are the questions,

00:39:35.239 --> 00:39:37.739
what are the three questions I need answered. If it's

00:39:37.739 --> 00:39:40.489
feedback, what are the three feedback questions is if I am

00:39:40.489 --> 00:39:43.489
trying to sell them on being our partner or paying us for

00:39:43.489 --> 00:39:46.239
something you know. There are key questions that I want to

00:39:46.239 --> 00:39:48.739
get answered in that direction and trying to get those

00:39:48.739 --> 00:39:51.239
answers and everything else is great in the meeting but

00:39:51.239 --> 00:39:52.489
that's how I handle.

00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:55.750
That I mean two things I would say one is I don't, getting

00:39:55.750 --> 00:39:58.750
started I don't think you need to do cold calls. You should

00:39:58.750 --> 00:40:01.500
have a network from the GSB and your friends there, take

00:40:01.500 --> 00:40:04.000
always more meetings and more interest and with everyone you

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:06.750
talk to they are going to realize they like the video

00:40:06.750 --> 00:40:09.500
whatever and they have people they get afraid to and then

00:40:09.500 --> 00:40:12.250
you have this nice path of going down just one more

00:40:12.250 --> 00:40:14.500
referrals. I think cold calls are pretty difficult in

00:40:14.500 --> 00:40:17.000
general. Another thing is just echo some male -- one thing

00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:19.500
someone told me in before fundraising which became very true

00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:22.750
was if you want money as per advice, if you want to advise

00:40:22.750 --> 00:40:25.750
that for money because they will be rather happy to give you

00:40:25.750 --> 00:40:28.250
feedback and if they are interested then they might follow

00:40:28.250 --> 00:40:31.250
up but the second you come to someone saying hey I am

00:40:31.250 --> 00:40:33.750
raising money, do you want to invest, people are just going

00:40:33.750 --> 00:40:34.750
to turn away.

