00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:10.500
I also want to ask you a question I think one of the most

00:42:10.500 --> 00:42:13.250
critical skills an entrepreneur can have is in sales and you

00:42:13.250 --> 00:42:15.500
obviously had some great training in an organization that

00:42:15.500 --> 00:42:17.819
has some of the sales training. What recommendations you

00:42:17.839 --> 00:42:20.839
have for people who don't have four years of IBM, and don't

00:42:20.839 --> 00:42:23.839
have that sales training how can they figure out I mean is

00:42:23.839 --> 00:42:26.299
it entrepreneur you are constantly so.

00:42:26.319 --> 00:42:34.389
Yeah so I will give you two things that I think are I will

00:42:34.409 --> 00:42:39.409
try and keep it quick. There are a few things. The first is

00:42:39.429 --> 00:42:42.509
you need to understand how your customers buy, your

00:42:42.529 --> 00:42:45.730
customers go through a buying process and if you are not

00:42:45.750 --> 00:42:48.349
sensitive to their buying process, you are just trying to

00:42:48.369 --> 00:42:52.049
close a deal. Not only you are going to close a deal you are

00:42:52.069 --> 00:42:55.569
going to piss them off and they are not going to talk to you

00:42:55.569 --> 00:42:58.319
ever again. And so what that means is your customers go

00:42:58.319 --> 00:43:01.069
through a very simple buying process which is okay well what

00:43:01.069 --> 00:43:04.069
do I really need, right what am I trying to accomplish what

00:43:04.069 --> 00:43:07.319
are my initiatives etc. And if you get to talk to them at

00:43:07.319 --> 00:43:10.069
that point when they are trying to figure out what exactly

00:43:10.069 --> 00:43:13.569
it is that they are trying to buy or you can help build a

00:43:13.569 --> 00:43:16.069
vision around what they actually need, based on the features

00:43:16.069 --> 00:43:19.069
that you have built. The second step in the process is once

00:43:19.069 --> 00:43:22.069
they kind of know what they need, then it's about okay well

00:43:22.069 --> 00:43:24.819
what are my options are, what are the different products I

00:43:24.819 --> 00:43:27.819
can buy or the solutions I can implement and that's when you

00:43:27.819 --> 00:43:30.319
traditionally do the pitching. And then once you go through

00:43:30.319 --> 00:43:32.819
that process then after they have seen everything and they

00:43:32.819 --> 00:43:35.569
have figured out if you are something that does make sense

00:43:35.569 --> 00:43:38.569
for what they need then you are going to closing mode. What

00:43:38.569 --> 00:43:41.319
everybody talks about is always be closing that I said don't

00:43:41.319 --> 00:43:44.069
list that. I hate that because customers don't react well to

00:43:44.069 --> 00:43:48.569
that. And then once you are in close mode we really clear

00:43:48.589 --> 00:43:51.190
with your customer that you are in close mode and try and

00:43:51.190 --> 00:43:55.859
close the deal. But I can probably go in for an hour on how

00:43:55.879 --> 00:43:58.629
you actually do that but it's you know when you started

00:43:58.629 --> 00:44:01.129
something complicated you said hey listen can we close this.

00:44:01.129 --> 00:44:04.129
When can you buy what you need to make the purchase and

00:44:04.129 --> 00:44:08.690
that's enough early on. The next thing is be brutal with

00:44:08.710 --> 00:44:12.279
your customers or at least your customer management and that

00:44:12.299 --> 00:44:15.130
listen if your customer is too small or your customer doesn'

00:44:15.150 --> 00:44:18.150
t have budget or your customer is planning on buying it in

00:44:18.150 --> 00:44:21.799
like 18 months stop talking of it. Just because it's these

00:44:21.819 --> 00:44:24.809
great brands doesn't mean you should waste all this time

00:44:24.829 --> 00:44:27.829
trying to get them to close with you if they don't budget

00:44:27.829 --> 00:44:30.079
around, timeframe you are talking about, person they don't

00:44:30.079 --> 00:44:33.079
really have a need. You are too busy so once you realize

00:44:33.079 --> 00:44:35.539
that someone doesn't have budget, authority, needs and time

00:44:35.539 --> 00:44:38.869
or timeframe move on to the next deal otherwise you are

00:44:38.889 --> 00:44:43.819
going to waste your time. Second to last thing, is start at

00:44:43.839 --> 00:44:48.599
the top, if you are selling to an organization start as high

00:44:48.619 --> 00:44:51.509
as you possibly can start in the organization. I think for

00:44:51.529 --> 00:44:55.329
rookies in sales it is too easy to convince yourself that oh

00:44:55.349 --> 00:44:59.099
I can get a meeting with this guy at a bottom so I am just

00:44:59.099 --> 00:45:01.849
going to do that, because the senior person won't want to

00:45:01.849 --> 00:45:04.849
talk to me and you start talking to that person what happens

00:45:04.849 --> 00:45:07.599
in an organization is at that low level person might give

00:45:07.599 --> 00:45:10.349
you a lot of great feedback, but they will generally believe

00:45:10.349 --> 00:45:12.849
that the are the authority on the purchase and they

00:45:12.849 --> 00:45:15.099
generally aren't. And once you build a relationship with

00:45:15.099 --> 00:45:17.599
them they might feel that they should be owning the

00:45:17.599 --> 00:45:20.599
relationship with you and if you try and get a meeting with

00:45:20.599 --> 00:45:23.099
someone in a different department or higher than them they

00:45:23.099 --> 00:45:26.349
might feel like you are going over the head and so you might

00:45:26.349 --> 00:45:28.849
have a political assurance on your head, which becomes a

00:45:28.849 --> 00:45:31.599
really big problem when your deal stalls. Now you can't talk

00:45:31.599 --> 00:45:34.849
to anyone else in trying to save the deals. And so deals can

00:45:34.849 --> 00:45:37.849
drag on in this case. The worst case scenario is you might

00:45:37.849 --> 00:45:41.349
lose a deal and you never you are going to know you lost it

00:45:41.349 --> 00:45:44.099
through talking to the wrong person. If you needed to talk

00:45:44.099 --> 00:45:47.099
that person can route you to the right person the moment he

00:45:47.099 --> 00:45:50.099
knows what you are selling. He is like oh, this is really

00:45:50.099 --> 00:45:53.099
interesting I want to learn more about it, Bob is the guy

00:45:53.099 --> 00:45:56.349
who is in-charge of this. And you meet with Bob and you did

00:45:56.349 --> 00:45:59.349
in one meeting, and now because Bob is going to write it

00:45:59.349 --> 00:46:02.849
down to one of his guys, he might write it down one of his

00:46:02.849 --> 00:46:05.849
guys, you might end up at the bottom, but now because you

00:46:05.849 --> 00:46:08.599
build a relationship with everybody on the way down if the

00:46:08.599 --> 00:46:11.849
deal stalls you can work the way back up. And the last thing

00:46:11.849 --> 00:46:15.099
is the most important thing a sales person can do is not the

00:46:15.099 --> 00:46:18.099
social, it's not be like fun person hanging out with, I am

00:46:18.099 --> 00:46:20.849
having a good pitch like all that stuff is pretty commodity

00:46:20.849 --> 00:46:23.349
everyone knows that, the most important thing is being able

00:46:23.349 --> 00:46:26.099
to answer a customer objection. When a customer says oh I

00:46:26.099 --> 00:46:28.599
don't want product, it's too expensive. And just go okay

00:46:28.599 --> 00:46:31.349
when customers tell you all the reasons they won't buy a

00:46:31.349 --> 00:46:33.849
product, what they are really doing is they are testing

00:46:33.849 --> 00:46:36.349
their understanding of what you are selling and whether or

00:46:36.349 --> 00:46:39.599
not they need it. So when they say oh it's too expensive, oh

00:46:39.599 --> 00:46:42.599
it's too big, oh it's slow whatever, you want to flash that

00:46:42.599 --> 00:46:45.349
idea. You want to understand where they are coming from or

00:46:45.349 --> 00:46:48.349
why do say it's too expensive. Well may be it's because they

00:46:48.349 --> 00:46:50.849
don't have budget, may be it's because they are comparing

00:46:50.849 --> 00:46:53.099
two different products. May be it's because they are

00:46:53.099 --> 00:46:55.349
comparing to some of the things completely irrelevant. You

00:46:55.349 --> 00:46:58.099
want to understand that stuff so that then you can formulate

00:46:58.099 --> 00:47:00.599
a response. Like well I understand you think it's too

00:47:00.599 --> 00:47:02.849
expensive, but if you consider this cost of building

00:47:02.849 --> 00:47:05.599
yourself which is what you are alternative really is this is

00:47:05.599 --> 00:47:08.599
actually price. And so you can bond to a lot of customer

00:47:08.599 --> 00:47:11.849
objections and if you do that your sales will go up. And by

00:47:11.849 --> 00:47:14.599
the way Harvard has a study that actually proved that that

00:47:14.599 --> 00:47:16.349
was the most effective thing for successful -

